    "note": "Read from the sheet. Line power enters at J1 (100-132V AC / 200-264V AC, 50-60 Hz, 30 VA), through the line filter FL1 and fuse F1 (100-132V 3/8A SB, 200-264V 3/16A SB) to terminals E7 LINE #1 and E9 LINE #2; E8 is the GRN/YEL chassis ground. S1 (220-240V / 100-120V) puts T1's two primaries (E10/E11 and E5/E6) in series or in parallel and S2 (100-220V / 120-240V) selects the 2ND TAP E16, so the four settings of Figure 4-5 are the four combinations. T1 has three shields -- E1 SHIELD #2 (WHT) on the guard bus with E15 GUARD and P3-1 / P3-6, E3 SHIELD #3 (GRA) as the C9 / C10 midpoint, E12 SHIELD #1 (GRN) on the chassis-ground bus with E8 and E13 -- and a CORE lead E14 that the test-time jumper ties to E13 (chassis) or to E15 GUARD. The single secondary E2 / E4 is rectified twice: bridge CR1 charges C1 (100 uF, 80 V) -- its + is TP3, its - is the TP4 / -RAW return, C2 0.1 uF across it -- and CR2 / CR3 from the two ends of the same winding charge the charger's own reservoir C3 (see BATT). C9 and C10 (0.05 uF) hang from E2 and E4 to the shield terminal E3 between them. Q1 (TIP120, an NPN Darlington) is the emitter follower: collector from TP3 through CR19, emitter through R1 0.5 ohm to TP6 and P3-2 (+RAW). Its base is held by a reference chain: current-regulator diodes CR25 and CR24 in series from TP3 (with CR4, a 40 V zener, across CR24) feed a reference node; CR6 carries that node to Q1's base; the node is clamped by CR5 in series with the 30 V zener CR10 down to the AC POWER LED node -- the node R9 (10 K from TP3) pulls up, CR12 (5.2 V zener) clamps to -RAW, and the front-panel AC PWR LED (A1 DS1, P3-4 + / P3-7 -) sits across it, so in the installed instrument that node rests at the LED's forward drop (about 2 V) and the reference is roughly 2 + 0.7 + 30 above -RAW, giving about 30-33 V at TP6 after CR6 and Q1's base-emitter drops -- 'approximately 32V dc' (§3-11), 32V dc in Table 4-3. P3-3 SWITCH CONTROL is the same LED node (it goes to A2 J3-3, J2-17, A4 P2-17, which the A4 sheet marks NC). CR7, CR8 and CR9 in series from Q1's base to the +RAW side of R1 limit the base drive once the drop across R1 plus Q1's base-emitter exceeds three diode drops: the pre-regulator's current limit. Nothing else on the board draws from +RAW; the charger has its own supply. -RAW (TP4, P3-8) is also the AC POWER LED return P3-7 and, at the connector, is drawn tied to P3-18 -BATTERY (see the caveat).",
