    "note": "§3-27 and §3-28 in the manual's words: Q2 is a current source that supplies all the charging current; Q3 and Q4 form a schmitt trigger; Q6 supplies a constant voltage output for trickle charging; during initial charging Q3 enables Q2 and the high charge rate; when the battery voltage rises to approximately 32V, Q4 turns off, shutting off the constant current charge, and the battery is constant voltage charged by Q6 (approximately 27V at 23°C); R10 sets the threshold point of this transition and hence the end of charge current; R20 sets the trickle voltage level; A3RT1 compensates it for ambient temperature; A6 RT1 / RT2 and Q5 prevent high current charging at temperatures below 5°C and/or high temperatures. Read from the sheet: the charger has its own reservoir -- CR2 (from E4) and CR3 (from E2) rectify the two ends of the secondary into C3 (330 uF, 80 V; its - end is on the TP4 return), so C3 charges to about the same peak as C1 (<=60 V). From C3's + line, R3 3.3 ohm feeds Q2's emitter (a PNP, 2N6125, on the heat sink with Q1) and DS1, the on-board LED, is the voltage reference in Q2's base circuit (§4-44 step 17 describes it as 'the voltage reference for the constant current source', calling it 'CR27'); R6 510 ohm runs from the DS1 / Q2-base node to Q3's collector, so while Q3 conducts the LED is lit and Q2 sources its constant current -- about 200 to 400 mA (Errata §4-45d), set by the LED drop less Q2's base-emitter across R3. R4 1.54 K from the supply, the germanium diode CR18 from Q2's base and the current-regulator diode CR20 meet at one node; CR20 goes on to Q6's collector (the trickle supply). Q2's collector is the charger output: through jumper W1 (upper circle) and CR13 to P3-9/10 +BATTERY, with Q6's emitter joining through CR16. The battery-voltage sense is TP2: the CR26 (current-regulator, 3 mA per errata Figure 12) cathode node, on the W1 lower-circle line to P3-11 (one end of A6 RT1); with W1 in, TP2 is the charger output itself, and with W1 out (§4-44 step 12) the rheostat between TP2 and TP1 stands in for the battery. From TP2, CR14 (5.2 V zener) drops to the top of the R12 16.2 K / R13 33.2 K / R14 17.4 K divider to -BATTERY; the R13 / R14 tap reaches Q4's base through CR23 (the diode the parts list and board call CR17) and R15 10 K, with C5 1 uF from the base node to -BATTERY. Q3 (FT317) and Q4 (2N5089) share an emitter return node: Q3's emitter through R7 22.6 ohm and Q4's emitter directly (no resistor) to a common node, then the 500 ohm trimpot R10 and the 5.6 V zener CR15 to -BATTERY -- R10 is the threshold adjustment of §4-44 steps 16-21. Q4's collector is Q3's base node, which CR11 in series with R8 (402 ohm; the sheet letters 4.02K) ties down to that emitter node and C4 4700 pF ties to Q3's collector; the node is fed through the current-regulator diode CR22 from the node that R11 (6.65 K on the sheet, 12.7 K in Table 5-4) hangs from TP2 and that Q5's base sits on. The BATTERY CHARGE LED (A1 DS2) is wired in parallel with R6: P3-13 (+) is the DS1-cathode / Q2-base node and P3-14 (-) is Q3's collector node, so the front-panel indicator and DS1 light together while Q3 conducts. Q5 (2N3906) is the temperature cut-off: its emitter is the CR14 anode node (TP2 less 5.2 V, the top of R12), its base the R11 / CR22 node, and its collector goes through the current-regulator diode CR21 into Q4's base node. The battery-pack thermistors hang across those two resistors: A6 RT1 (P3-11 = the TP2 line, P3-12 = the Q5 base node) is in parallel with R11, and A6 RT2 (P3-15 = the top of R12, P3-16 = the R12 / R13 tap, 'THERMISTOR VOLTAGE COMPENSATION') is in parallel with R12. A cold or hot battery raises RT1, the drop across R11 || RT1 (fed by CR22's 1 mA) then exceeds CR14's 5.2 V, Q5 turns on and forces the Schmitt trigger out of the high-rate state; RT2 shifts the sense-divider ratio and so the switching threshold with battery temperature. Trickle: CR28 (0.47 mA current regulator) from the charger supply into TP5, which is Q6's base; TP5 sits on RT1 10 K in parallel with R17 6.49 K, then R18 43.2 K (and, from Rev F, R19 15 K) and the 50 K trimpot R20 to -BATTERY, C6 0.01 uF from TP5 to -BATTERY; R20 sets TP5 to 33.0 V dc (§4-44 step 10). Q6 (2N2484) is an emitter follower from that reference: emitter through CR16 to +BATTERY, R16 10 K from emitter to base, collector supplied through CR20. The front-panel BTRY CHG LED (A1 DS2, P3-13 + / P3-14 -) is driven from the charger's control side and lights in the constant-current state (§1-6, §2-24: on steadily for normal charging, off when the battery is charged; Errata #7: blinks if the battery is very low). Errata §4-45d: constant current 200-400 mA until about 31 V, then constant voltage (27V) for a few milliamps trickle; Errata #12 (step 27): 25.8 to 27 V at the battery in trickle mode, adjust R20 if not.",
